  "profile_id": "hk-chicken-v2",
  "version": 2,
  "description": "Chicken-hand rules, 13-tile Hong Kong Mahjong. The same as HKMA Classical (cap 10, flowers do not score, no Seven Pairs) with two changes. A complete hand with no scoring pattern, a chicken hand, may win: the minimum is 0 faan. And every win pays the same, whatever its faan, whoever paid for the tile: each of the other three seats pays 1 and the winner collects 3, whether the win was self-drawn or off a discard (the discarder pays no more than the others). Faan are still found and logged, but they do not change the payment. See RULES.md.",
  "derived_from": {
    "profile": "hk-hkma-v1",
    "rules_hash": "43e4e01c50dce4d3",
    "change": "win.minimum_faan is 0 instead of 3, and the payment is flat: every row of the payment table is 1, the self-draw multiplier is 3 and the discarder pays the same as the other two losers, so every win moves 3 points to the winner, 1 from each other seat. Nothing else changes."
  },
